hello everyone and welcome to the  seventh annual Academy of Motion Picture  Arts and Sciences governor's Awards  we're delighted that you could join us  for this ceremony which is dedicated to  individuals whose careers have  transformed our industry and set a  standard of excellence admired around  the world I do feel it's important to  mention yesterday's horrifying attacks  in Paris and say that all of us here  stand in solidarity and support of  France and the French people  we may be in Hollywood tonight but the  Academy is an institution that  celebrates film wherever it is made our  connection with the film loving French  is especially deep with waves of  influence flowing back and forth across  the Atlantic  ever since the Lumiere brothers made the  first moving pictures so as we gather  here to celebrate our history and some  of the people who have made it we also  mourn those who died we send our deepest  affection to our brothers and sisters  and France before we turn the focus to  tonight's honorees I want to take this  opportunity to address an important  conversation which is going on in the  motion picture community and across the  country today it's a conversation about  recognizing and embracing a broad and  diverse cross-section of talent  something that I know all of you care  deeply about  I'm talking about diversity of age  gender race national origin and point of  view what Shonda Rhimes rightfully calls  the normalization of showbusiness a  process that needs to continue if we are  to faithfully represent the audience  which we serve you the people in this  room are the true movers and shakers of  our industry you understand that when it  comes to fair and equal representation  in our industry words are not enough we  also have a responsibility to take  action and we have a unique opportunity  to do so now interest in the motion  picture arts and sciences has never been  as strong as it is today the world is  watching to see how we respond to this  critical issue at the academy we want to  do our part to make this right this past  year we brought in a more diverse class  of new members than ever before this  incoming class of members doesn't just  include new talent but also includes  women and people of color and of varied  ethnicities who had been overlooked in  the past  in addition today 17 of our 51 governors  are women  but we want to do more than that we know  that the Academy is uniquely positioned  to take the lead on this issue to that  end we've started a new Academy  initiative a 2020 a five-year plan to  build on these efforts and to take  concrete measures to improve the  diversity of our staff and governance as  well as how we elect our leadership and  bring in new voices but we can't stop  there and we can't continue this effort  without your help this must truly be an  industry-wide commitment you have been  tremendous partners to the Academy since  our inception and in all our initiatives  to preserve the past honor the present  and shape the future of our industry we  ask you to partner with us again on this  critically important initiative many of  you our Academy members and as  ambassadors of our industry are in  positions of power to hire mentor  encourage and promote talent in all  areas of our profession I'm asking you  tonight directly to be our partners on  this critically important initiative  tonight we are honoring three  distinguished artists who represent both  Hollywood in its golden era an  independent cinema at its most cutting  edge and I'm pleased that this year two  of our honorees happen to be women and  one an african-american man Debbie  Reynolds Jenner Rollins and Spike Lee  follow very different  they follow very different trajectories  to preeminence but they are united by a  love of this art form you're going to  hear much more about them tonight from  their peers for now I want to simply  raise the glass to these three  remarkable artists and their exceptional  contributions to our profession okay  Cheers they are all an inspiration to us  all everyone stand please  to the three of you Debbie  Jenna and Spike thank you for your  outstanding bodies of work and the  legacies you have given us thank you  Cheers
 

